## 1️⃣ Test Way 1: SQL Injection (SQLi) via Registration Parameters
This attempts to break the database query logic during account creation to read information from the database or execute arbitrary commands. [1] 

* 🎯 Target Parameters: username, email, phone, promo_code. [2] 
* 📋 Step-by-Step Execution:
1. Open Burp Suite and capture a standard account registration request to https://1win.com.
   2. Send the request to Burp Repeater.
   3. Inject logical SQL breaking characters into the registration input fields. [3, 4] 
* 💉 Payloads:
* Time-Based Blind SQLi: 'XOR(if(now()=sysdate(),sleep(5),0))XOR'
   * Error-Based SQLi: ' OR EXTRACTVALUE(1, CONCAT(0x7e, (SELECT @@version)))-- [5] 
* 🔍 Response Verification Criteria: Hit Send. A vulnerability is confirmed if the response delays significantly (matching your sleep duration) or returns a database system error containing sensitive server data. [6, 7] 
* 💰 Policy Match / Reward: Injections (SQLi or equivalent) — $1,500 USD (Critical Severity)

